                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+2-category"} monoidal 2-category
                    (with some duality and strictness structure)
            %p
              %strong
                3-Tannaka duality for
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+2-categories"} module 2-categories
                over
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+2-categories"} monoidal 2-categories
            %table
              %thead
                %tr
                  %th
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+2-category"} monoidal 2-category
                  %th
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-category+of+module+2-categories"} 3-category of module 2-categories
              %tbody
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Mod
                            %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod_A
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi R
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                    \-
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-algebra"} 3-algebra
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Mod
                            %mi R
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod_R
                    \-
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4-module"} 4-module
          %h5#MatrixCaclulusFor2Modules Matrix calculus for 2-modules: Bimodules and Eilenberg-Watts theorem
          %p
            If a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒱
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V} \coloneqq Mod_R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
            serves as a 2-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/basis"} basis
            for a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod_R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-module"} 2-module
            by the
            %a{:href => "#BasesFor2ModulesAndTannakaDualityForAssociativeAlgebras"} above
            discussion, there should be an analog of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrix+calculus"} matrix calculus
            to present 2-linear maps between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-modules"} 2-modules
            equipped with such a 2-basis.
          %p
            Such a higher
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrix"} matrix
            is what in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
            is called a
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒱
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V}
              \-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profunctor"} profunctor
            (or “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributor"}> distributor
            ”): a profunctor between
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒱
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi 𝒱
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}_1, \mathcal{A}_2 \in \mathcal{V}Cat
            is a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒱
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor"} enriched functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msubsup
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mn 1
                    %mi op
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mn 2
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒱
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  K
                  \\;\colon\;
                  \\mathcal{A}_1^{op}
                  \\times
                  \\mathcal{A}_2
                  \\to
                  \\mathcal{V}
                  \\,.
          %p
            Compare this to how a matrix between two vector spaces equipped with basis sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_1, B_2
            is a function
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mn 2
                  %mo →
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  K \colon B_1 \times B_2 \to k
          %p
            to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [B_1,k]
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \colon B_1 \to k
            is given by the vector
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mn 2
                  %mo →
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K v \colon B_2 \to k
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ↦
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi b
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mn 1
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  b_2 \mapsto \sum_{b_1 \in B_1} v(b_1) \cdot K(b_1,b_2)
                  \\,.
          %p
            If we replace in this formula the sum by a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coend"} coend
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profunctor"} profunctor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            on a
            = succeed "-functor" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒱
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒱
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \colon \mathcal{A}_1 \to \mathcal{V}
            to yield
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mn 2
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒱
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \otimes v \colon \mathcal{A}_2 \to \mathcal{V}
            with
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ↦
                  %msup
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mn 1
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  a_2 \mapsto \int^{a_1 \in A_1} v(a_1) \otimes K(a_1, a_2)
                  \\,.
          %p
            For the case at hand where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒱
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Mod
                    %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V} = Mod_R
            and in the special case that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}_1 = \mathbf{B}A_1
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒜
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}_2 = \mathbf{B}A_2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ×
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 2
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒱
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}A_1 \times \mathbf{B}A_2 \to \mathcal{V}
            is equivalently an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_1
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo −
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A-2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bimodule"} bimodule
            in the traditional sense of associative algebra. Moreover, the
            = succeed "-action" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coend"} coend
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+modules"} tensor product of modules
            over the given algebra. Motivated by this example one also generally calls profunctors “bimodules”.
          %p
            Now one should ask to which extent these “2-matrices” given by profunctors capture all the 2-linear maps between
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-modules"} 2-modules
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Watts+theorem"} Eilenberg-Watts theorem
            solves:
          #EilenbergWattsTheorem.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              There is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+equivalence"} natural
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mn 2
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi Ab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (-) \otimes_{A_1} (-)
                    \\;\colon\;
                    {}_{A_1} Mod_{A_2}
                    \\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                    Hom_{2Ab}(Mod_{A_1}, Mod_{A_2})
            %p
              between
              = succeed "-preserving" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod_{A_1} \to Mod_{A_2}
              between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+of+modules"} categories of modules
              and
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_1
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo −
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A-2
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bimodules"} bimodules
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
              functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mn 1
                    %mi N
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (-) \otimes_{A_1} N \;\colon\; Mod_{A_1} \to Mod_{A_2}
                    \\,.
          %p
            In summary we this find that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Mod
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Mod
                        %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod_{Mod_R}
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod_R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-modules"} 2-modules
            with 2-basis is equivalent to the 2-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Prof
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Mod
                    %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Prof(Mod_R)
            of
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod_R
            = succeed "." do
